      "data": {
        "kind": "start",
        "title": "On the sand",
        "description": "The player and Kell stand on the sand by the gate; across it, whoever they've picked to fight. Let the far side speak first (Sallow, if he's there, is courteous about it; the Crakes discuss their rates; the dogs don't) and let the player answer, briefly. The ring is for fighting: the first blow, the first weapon drawn, or the first step towards each other starts it.",
        "cast": {
          "kell": "At the investigator's shoulder, truncheon out: one dry word, if any.",
          "sallow": "Courteous, superior, pulling on his gloves: he regrets that this will have to be settled the other way.",
          "crake-1": "Rolling his shoulders, quoting his rates.",
          "crake-2": "Rolling his shoulders, saying nothing."
        },
        "lore": []
      }
    },
